Theorem TF-1: Scalar literal transfer produces SCALAR sentinel

  Preconditions:
    - Instruction is `Let { Literal(kind) }` per Annex E §AIMS TF-1
    - `kind` ranges over the scalar literal categories enumerated in §3 TF-1:
      int / float / bool / char / byte / duration / size / Ordering / unit / Never
    - SCALAR is the sentinel per Annex E §AIMS L-9 — NOT a lattice element

  Soundness property:
    Forall literal kinds k. transfer_tf1(Let { Literal(k) }) = SCALAR
    AND L-6 layer (b) monotonicity holds for the constant function f(_) = SCALAR.

  Proof obligation:
    Two-part discharge:
      (a) Output enumeration — for each of the 10 literal kinds, the forward
          transfer rule per Appendix A row 1 emits `dst.state := SCALAR` on
          every per-dimension column (Access / Consumption / Cardinality /
          Uniqueness / Locality / Shape / Effect all = SCALAR).
      (b) L-6 layer (b) monotonicity — TF-1 is a constant function: for ANY
          pair of input states (a, b) with a ≤ b, f(a) = f(b) = SCALAR; by
          L-4 reflexivity SCALAR ≤ SCALAR, hence f(a) ≤ f(b).

    Part (a) — literal-kind enumeration (10 kinds per Annex E §AIMS TF-1):
      int / float / bool / char / byte — primitive scalar payloads, no RC;
      duration / size — unit-tagged 64-bit integer payloads, no RC;
      Ordering — three-variant enum {Less, Equal, Greater}, payload-free;
      unit — singleton `()`, payload-free;
      Never — uninhabited bottom type, never constructed but kind enumerable.
      All 10 collapse to the SCALAR sentinel row in Appendix A.

    Part (b) — constant-function monotonicity:
      Constant f(_) = c is trivially monotone: forall a, b. f(a) = f(b) = c,
      and c ≤ c by L-4 reflexivity. SCALAR ≤ SCALAR holds definitionally
      (the only valid comparison on SCALAR per L-9 — incomparability with
      non-SCALAR states is intentional and not in this proof's scope).

    Engines dispatched:
      monotonicity (PRIMARY — L-6 layer (b) per-rule discharge per
        section_04::verify_tf1_scalar_literal — constant-function check)
      case_analysis (PRIMARY — Appendix A row 1 forward-transfer enumeration
        across 10 literal kinds per section_04::verify_tf1_scalar_literal)
      lattice (SECONDARY — accepts gracefully; primary engines discharged)
      refinement (SECONDARY — accepts gracefully; refinement is TF-6 / TF-6a
        territory, not TF-1)

  Expected:
    status: valid
    reason: section_04 monotonicity + case_analysis engines discharge TF-1 via 10-kind literal enumeration + constant-function monotonicity check
